 ## Background
-Fourier positional encoding was introduced in the context of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) by Mildenhall et al. in 2020 [S2]. It was adopted to enable the MLP to represent high-frequency details in natural images. The method is inspired by the use of sinusoidal positional encodings in Transformer architectures, but adapted for continuous coordinate representation. It is a key component in many neural rendering pipelines, including SIREN-based methods, where it helps the network learn high-frequency scene details [S1, S4].
